course: dictionary
lesson: 11494
title: Aggression
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Aggression is a noun, and you will meet it in lessons about feelings, behaviour and history. It means angry or violent behaviour or feelings that make a person or animal want to attack or hurt others. «The dog showed aggression when a stranger came near its puppies.» The dog was not just cross. It was ready to attack to protect them.
explain: Use the words around it to work out the meaning. «Ben's aggression made the game unsafe, because he kicked and pushed his friends.» Kicking and pushing are clues that aggression means violent behaviour. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Ben's angry, violent behaviour made the game unsafe.» It still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Aggression can be a feeling you notice inside yourself. «Signs of aggression» include clenched fists, a loud voice and hot red cheeks. Spotting these signs helps you calm down before you hurt someone. Aggression can also be words. «Verbal aggression», such as shouting insults, can hurt people as much as hitting.
explain: The word also appears in history and sport. In history, «an act of aggression» is when one country attacks another without being attacked first, and it can start a war. In sport, aggression can mean playing with great force and energy, which is fine as long as it stays fair.
fact: Aggression means angry or violent behaviour or feelings that make someone want to attack or hurt others.
fact: In history, an act of aggression is when a country attacks another without being attacked first.
fact: Animals show aggression to protect their food or their young.
fact: In sport, aggression can mean playing with great force and energy.
fact: Verbal aggression means hurting someone with angry words.
exercise: «The dog showed aggression when a stranger came near its puppies.» What does aggression mean here? | Happy and wagging its tail | A loud noise from a far-off field | *Angry behaviour, ready to attack to protect its young | Sleepy after a long day
exercise: Which phrase means hurting someone with angry words? | Calm and quiet | *Verbal aggression | Signs of tiredness | An act of aggression
exercise: In history, what can «an act of aggression» start? | A new park | *A war | A school trip | A birthday party
test: «Ella felt aggression rising, so she counted to ten and walked away.» What does aggression mean here? | Happy excitement | A sleepy, quiet mood | Hunger after lunch | *Angry feelings that could make her want to hurt someone
test: In sport, what can aggression mean? | *Playing with great force and energy | Sitting still on the bench | Losing every game | Cheating and breaking the rules
exam: Which statement about aggression is correct? | Aggression is always a kind, calm feeling | Aggression is a type of food | Aggression only means being very tired | *Aggression can be angry behaviour, an attack by a country, or playing with great force
